					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-27 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="430">
  <tbody><tr>
    <td width="200" align="center" valign="top"><a href="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/flyers/bambuflyerback-flat.jpg"><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/flyers/bambuflyerweb.jpg" border="0" alt="" width="200" height="446" /></a></td>
    <td width="15">&nbsp;</td>
    <td width="215" align="left" valign="top"><p class="body1"><font size="1">Big up to the comrade <strong>Bambu</strong> (Native Guns) on the release of his new album <em><strong>I Scream Bars for the Children</strong></em>. This Sunday (4/29), Sabzi and I head down to Los Angeles to celebrate the album release with a <strong>Block Party in Historic Filipinotown</strong> featuring <strong>Ise Lyfe</strong>, <strong>The Attik</strong>, <strong>Eye A Sage</strong>, <strong>The Committee</strong> and special guests. And of course, <strong>Bam</strong> himself with <strong>DJ Phatrick</strong>. </font></p>
<font size="1">    </font><p class="body1"><font size="1">If you can&#39;t make it to the show,  you can order the album online at <a href="http://www.beatrock.com" target="new"><strong>www.beatrock.com</strong></a>. The album is hot and the brotha reps hard for  Pinoys and Pinays everwhere. Plus, I got a verse on that joint. Cop it! </font></p>
<font size="1">    </font><p class="body1"><font size="1">See you in LA!</font></p>
<font size="1">    </font><p class="body1"><font size="1"><strong><span class="style2">SUNDAY, APRIL 29</span><br />
      The Power and Potential<br />
      of the Youth BLOCK PARTY
      </strong><br />
      feat. Bambu, Ise Lyfe, Blue Scholars,<br />
      Attik, Eye A Sage, The Committee,<br />
      and special guests!
      <br />
      <strong>LOS ANGELES, CA
      </strong><br />
  12pm to 6pm <br />
  in Echo Park/Historic
  Filipinotown<br /> 
  (Rosemont Ave. &amp; Temple St.)<br />
  $10 donation</font>
    </p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-26 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><p class="body1">Hello world. Your comrade Geo is back on the blog. Finally back home from three school shows in three days on the East Coast. From <strong>Peddie High</strong> to <strong>Columbia University</strong> to <strong>Lehigh</strong> and back to NYC, it&#39;s good to see young students of color holding it down on their respective campuses. Also helps to have down-ass teachers (right. <strong>Mr. Hiebert</strong>?). Peace to <strong>Ryan (Heiroku)</strong> at Columbia who we learned was one of the students who took part in last October&#39;s <strong>Minutemen Project</strong> <strong>protest</strong> (<a href="../smf/index.php?topic=66.0">posted in the Forums</a>).</p>
      <p class="style1">Also, we got a chance to chill with <strong>Noah</strong> at <strong>WFMU</strong> to talk about the upcoming album (June 12!), Seattle hip-hop and even bust a quick semi-freestyle. You can check the audio at <a href="http://www.wfmu.org/playlists/NU">wfmu.org</a> (scroll down to April 18, 2007). Keep listener-supported radio alive!</p>
      <p class="style1">Lastly, big up to <strong>Ralph</strong> from <strong>Kicksclusive</strong> for hookin us up with some of the latest <strong>Kilo Goods</strong> and <strong>Rocksmith</strong> gear and making <strong>Sabzi</strong> a very happy man (I&#39;m good with rockin&#39; all-over neon and pastel colors - thanks tho homies).</p>
      <p class="style1">I love the fresh Northwest air. Almost makes the constant cloud cover worth it.</p>
      <p class="style1">Easy<br />
      Geo</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-23 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>peace, kinfolk.&nbsp; one week after the tragic event to be known henceforth as the &quot;VT Massacre,&quot;&nbsp;i&nbsp;trust your hearts and minds have taken some time to heal.&nbsp;&nbsp; and in the process of grieving i&nbsp;hope your reflections have led you to the understanding that no act of violence is ever senseless, but systemic.&nbsp;&nbsp; may we begin to think critically about the individual role we play in this&nbsp;increasingly aggressive&nbsp;society, and work diligently to spread among our compatriots a sense of honor, love and trust in one another; we truly are the keepers of our brothers.<br /><br />your&nbsp;entire massline fam&nbsp;getting set to hit the road with this message of accountability and interdependence -- check the updated tour schedule and holla ever-so-loudly when we whirlwind through your city:<br /><br />5/16/2007 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />Berbati&rsquo;s Pan<br />231 SW Ankeny St. <br />Portland, OR 97204<br /><a href="http://www.berbati.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.berbati.com/</font></a> <br /><br />5/17/07<br />Hells Kitchen <br />3829 6th Ave. <br />Tacoma, WA 98406<br />6PM &ndash; All Ages<br />9PM &ndash; 21+<br /><a href="http://www.hellskitchenonline.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.hellskitchenonline.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/18/07<br />Raw Sushi<br />523 W 1st Ave<br />Spokane, WA 99201<br />21+ - doors 10PM<br /><a href="http://www.spokanesushi.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.spokanesushi.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/19/07<br />The Loft<br />418 N. Higgins Ave.<br />Missoula, MT 59801<br />18+<br /><a href="http://www.myspace.com/theloftmissoula" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.myspace.com/theloftmissoula</font></a> <br /><br />5/20/07<br />Zebra Cocktail Lounge<br />321 E Main St.<br />Bozeman, MT 59715<br />21+<br /><a href="http://www.zebracocktaillounge.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.zebracocktaillounge.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/21/07<br />Neurolux<br />111 N. 11th St.<br />Boise, ID 83702<br />21+<br /><a href="http://www.neurolux.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.neurolux.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/22/07<br />Urban Lounge<br />241 S 500 E<br />Salt Lake City, UT 84102<br />21+ - $10<br /><a href="http://www.myspace.com/theurbanlounge" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.myspace.com/theurbanlounge</font></a><br /><br /><br />5/26/07<br />Sasquatch Music Festival<br />Gabe Teodros<br />Quincy, WA. <br /><a href="http://sasquatchfestival.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://sasquatchfestival.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/27/07<br />Sasquatch Music Festival<br />Common Market<br />Quincy, WA. <br /><a href="http://sasquatchfestival.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://sasquatchfestival.com/</font></a> <br /><br />5/28/07<br />The Hidden House<br />607 W Osborn Rd.<br />Phoenix, AZ 85257<br />21+ doors 9PM<br /><a href="http://www.myspace.com/thehiddenhouse" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">www.myspace.com/thehiddenhouse</font></a><br /><br />5/29/07&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />Hot Monkey Love<br />6875 El Cajon Blvd.<br />San Diego, CA<br />All Ages<br /><a href="http://www.hotmonkeylovecafe.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.hotmonkeylovecafe.com</font></a><br /><br />5/30/07<br />Knitting Factory LA<br />7021 Hollywood Boulevard <br />Los Angeles, CA 90028<br />All Ages<br />$11 &ndash; doors 9PM<br /><a href="http://www.knittingfactory.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.knittingfactory.com/</font></a><br /><br />5/31/07<br />Poleng<br />1751 Fulton St. <br />San Francisco, CA<br />21+<br /><a href="http://www.polenglounge.com/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.polenglounge.com/</font></a><br /><br />6/2/07<br />Grove<br />1033 NW Bond St.<br />Bend, OR<br /><a href="http://www.thegrove411.net/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.thegrove411.net/</font></a><br /><br />6/3/07<br />Wow Hall<br />291 W 8th Ave<br />Eugene, OR 97401<br />All Ages<br />$10 &ndash; doors 8:30PM<br /><a href="http://www.wowhall.org/" target="_blank"><font color="#727272">http://www.wowhall.org/</font></a><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-15 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><u><strong>Gabriel Teodros&#39; video shoot for &quot;No Label&quot;!</strong></u><br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/239/459406237_4f9eb7b1be.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" /><br />Jose Rizal Bridge<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/202/459384762_bfc01518a1.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" /><br />&quot;The Block&quot; (20th and Pearl)<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/190/459431600_c4335c5506.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" /><br />Beacon Elementary!<br /><br />Keep visiting this site for more info on the video&#39;s premier!<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<br /><br />[all photos taken by daps1]<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-13 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><strong>&quot;No Label (Esma Remix)&quot;</strong> the first single from <strong>Gabriel Teodros&#39;</strong> solo masterpiece, <strong>Lovework</strong>, will be made into a <strong>music video</strong> this weekend.  <br /><strong><br />Saturday, April 14th, 2007,</strong> MassLine invites you to participate in the production of this video at <strong>Beacon Hill Elementary School</strong>, beginning at <strong>1:00pm</strong>.  with a song that serves to represent the community that our homie GT came up in, it is only appropriate that the community is there.  come out, show your face and support!<br /><br />make sure you arrive on time!<br /><br />when you come through, be sure to have the video release form signed and ready to give to the crew.  this is absolutely necessary, as the video will be broadcast on national television when it is complete.<br /><br />download the video release form <a href="http://www.bluescholars.com/bay/VideoReleaseForm.pdf"> <strong>here</strong></a>.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="a